---
/* L02 - the wire protocol: state in, answers out, one normalised shape.
   One writer: the figures workstream E. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L02.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a hotel reception counter where a guest slides a folded note and a blank slip across to a clerk, who hands back a blank card divided into four small compartments."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L02-fig-title L02-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L02-fig-title">State in, answers out, one normalised shape</title>
      <desc id="L02-fig-desc">
        Three panels left to right. The first is the request: three keys, model, state and questions,
        with the state written as a plain sentence. The second is what different providers send back:
        one card typed noul with a value of 0.9, one typed boolean with a value of true, and one
        typed value with a value of 0.9. The third is the normalised shape: one answer box with four
        compartments, kind, value, probabilities and confidence, holding kind noul, value 0.9, an
        empty probabilities compartment and a null confidence. An arrow draws itself along the wire
        from the request to the answers and another from the answers to the normalised shape, and a
        prussian dot pulses once beside the normalised kind.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="L02-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--color-ink-45)" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- 1. the request -->
      <rect x="24" y="52" width="168" height="176" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="36" y="74" class="fig-head">the request</text>
      <text x="36" y="102" class="fig-key">model</text>
      <text x="36" y="122" class="fig-key">state</text>
      <text x="36" y="142" class="fig-key">questions</text>
      <text x="104" y="102" class="fig-text">jev-latest</text>
      <text x="104" y="122" class="fig-text">a sentence</text>
      <text x="104" y="142" class="fig-text">three</text>
      <line x1="36" y1="160" x2="180" y2="160" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="36" y="180" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">three keys, always</text>
      <text x="36" y="196" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">the state is data,</text>
      <text x="36" y="212" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">never an instruction</text>

      <!-- 2. what comes back over the wire -->
      <rect x="228" y="52" width="184" height="176" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="240" y="74" class="fig-head">what comes back</text>
      <rect x="240" y="88" width="160" height="30" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="248" y="107" class="fig-text">type noul</text>
      <text x="392" y="107" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">0.9</text>
      <rect x="240" y="124" width="160" height="30" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="248" y="143" class="fig-text">type boolean</text>
      <text x="392" y="143" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">true</text>
      <rect x="240" y="160" width="160" height="30" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="248" y="179" class="fig-text">type value</text>
      <text x="392" y="179" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">0.9</text>
      <text x="240" y="212" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">three shapes for one idea</text>

      <!-- 3. the normalised shape -->
      <rect x="448" y="52" width="168" height="176" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="460" y="74" class="fig-head">normalised</text>
      <rect x="460" y="88" width="144" height="30" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="468" y="107" class="fig-text">kind</text>
      <text x="580" y="107" class="fig-num fig-num--prussian" text-anchor="end">noul</text>
      <circle class="m-pulse" style="--m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 1.2s;" cx="590" cy="103" r="3.5" fill="var(--color-prussian)" />
      <rect x="460" y="122" width="144" height="30" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="468" y="141" class="fig-text">value</text>
      <text x="596" y="141" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">0.9</text>
      <rect x="460" y="156" width="144" height="30" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="468" y="175" class="fig-text">probabilities</text>
      <text x="596" y="175" class="fig-num fig-text--dim" text-anchor="end">empty</text>
      <rect x="460" y="190" width="144" height="30" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="468" y="209" class="fig-text">confidence</text>
      <text x="596" y="209" class="fig-num fig-text--dim" text-anchor="end">null</text>

      <!-- the wire, and the one idea of motion: the answer travels the wire and
           arrives as one normalised answer -->
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 32; --m-duration: 1.3s;" d="M 192 140 L 224 140" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L02-arrow)" />
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 32; --m-duration: 1.3s; --m-delay: 0.6s;" d="M 412 140 L 444 140" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L02-arrow)" />

      <!-- the rule the whole harness rests on -->
      <rect x="24" y="256" width="592" height="60" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="40" y="280" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">the state is data; the instructions live on our slip, not in the note</text>
      <text x="40" y="300" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">normalise at the adapter, and every metric reads the same four keys</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L02</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">Three keys go out and three different answer shapes come back, but the adapter folds them into one answer box with the same four keys, which is the only interface the metrics ever see.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .fig-head {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-key {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-text--ink {
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-text--dim {
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-num--prussian {
    fill: var(--color-prussian);
  }
</style>
